r all the scenes with shrunken alice  there's a small detail about the mad  hatter's appearance that you may have  overlooked  his eyes are larger than normal the vfx  team  actually manually enhanced their size in  post-production  this was a small yet important feature  that helped portray the character's odd  quirky style it's you  one of the most iconic scenes in the  original alice in wonderland is when she  shrinks and grows  so recreating it in the live action  version was an important scene  they used a mix of cg elements live  action and camera tricks to achieve the  effects  when alice shrinks the entire room is cg  along with alice's body  for when she grows big the crew built a  small set that made mia vashikawska  appear to be giant it's only a dream one  of the funniest yet ten  scenes in the film comes when the red  queen is interrogating her frog's  servants  the behind the scenes is even funnier  with red queen actress helena bonham  carter  speaking to green frog statues it's odd  to look at  and will definitely change the way you  view this scene  the cheshire cat is one of the most  unique characters in the film  especially with regards to how he moves  and interacts with the  environment it was a completely cgi  character  created by the movie's vfx team and when  cheshire interacted with alice  there was a person in a green screen  suit as a stand-in  performing the action i never get  involved in politics  knave of hearts is a very tall character  which required some effects trickery to  achieve  actor crispin glover was on stilts the  entire time he was filming for this  character  the effects team then digitally extended  his limbs in post creating the lanky  character we see on screen  this is a perfect example of how  practical effects and digital  alterations  can work together in harmony you're all  mad  the mad hatter execution scene featured  a lot of characters and actors  and was a challenge to film the crowd  was shot separately from the principal  actors  and the environment was completely cg  senior visual effects supervisor  ken ralston explained what made it so  difficult  the execution scene was a challenge for  all the different interaction of the  characters  live action characters animated  characters hybrid characters like the  tweedles and stain  the magical land of wonderland is full  of stunning  visuals and beautiful colors in the  movie it was completely created with cg  when alice first enters wonderland the  only real elements  are her and the staircase she is walking  on the vfx team did a great job  creating the mystical land and giving it  a memorable look  wait this is my dream alice through the  looking glass introduced us to  characters that represent  seconds of time it's a unique concept  that the vfx  team built from the ground up we also  see the seconds combined to 4 minutes  which then combine to form hours this  means the minutes and hours are made up  of the individual  seconds characters these miniscule  artisans are my  seconds when alice travels back in time  she finds the mad hatter roaming around  in town surprisingly this was actually a  practical set that they built  the only vfx used were to create the sky  and background  it's one of the few times they actually  used more of a practical set for a  wonderland scene  and it looks great have we missed the  second time  alice enters wonderland she enters a  room that is a lot more stocked than the  shrinking room in the first movie  it looks like a normal room with some  wonderland flair  but it may surprise you to learn that  the entire room was computer generated  alice was shot on a blue screen and the  room was animated in post-production  what has happened in the same room alice  enters after going through the mirror  there is a giant chess board she lands  on the chess pieces are completely cg  so to give vasikowska the correct line  of sight they had people in green screen  suits holding up  giant pole